{"t": 20.81, "agent": "legal", "type": "answer", "text": "Yes, from a legal standpoint the Gripworks MSA is ready to sign this week: the draft (v3) has Net-45 payment, a 12-month term, and a liability cap of 1x fees, and all redlines were resolved on Sep 20 \u2014 verified in our records with high freshness. \n\nGap: I could not identify or reach any finance-side (payment/budget approval) or engineering-side (technical dependency) stations for Gripworks to confirm there's no blocker outside legal's scope \u2014 those station names aren't known to me, so I wasn't able to hand off to finance or eng for confirmation. If a finance sign-off is required before execution, that should be checked separately.", "citations": ["legal/gripworks-msa"], "run": "ufo-claude-1"}
